  "discharged_interface_obligations": [
    "Linear cons heads on an authenticated proper spine now have a full conditional observer node contract preserving a restricted ground replacement set and finite attached execution.",
    "The recursive successor freshness rule no longer needs post-unification finiteness as an independent premise: it is derived from finite incoming call, proper spine, head linearity and arity.",
    "The actual tail-coordinate map carries a spine length exactly one less than the incoming spine."
  ],
  "checked_operational_obligations": [
    "Successful cons resolution provides an actual matching witness even when symbolic matching is unavailable.",
    "Caller leaf effects and finite execution are preserved on attached base transitions including failure and saved alternatives.",
    "Parameter relation and free body-only output separation hold in the same actual successor valuation.",
    "Full node contract retains complete successor initialization, scope restoration and strict residual descent."
  ],
  "actual_rows": [
    "0:23",
    "35:3"
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
    "Proper incoming spine and complete success/failure conditions remain source-family premises.",
    "Finite spine length alone does not establish finite elements; incoming finite call and attached caller finiteness remain explicit.",
    "Separation is established from the instantiated selected call; additional caller values still need their own coverage and finiteness facts.",
    "Fixtures validate source actions and structural premises, not unconditional source-node acceptance or full runtime invariants.",
    "Caller-slot controls are synthetic executable examples, not production witnesses.",
    "Tail decrement does not replace strict residual descent or discharge recursive references.",
    "Existing pinned extraction tables are reused; no fresh native extraction or production source certification."
  ],
